@startuml proximity-detection
title US-05: Proximity Detection - No Prior Relationship Check via Neo4j

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Kafka
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as Correlation
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j
participant "Alert\nEvaluator\n(leader)" as Evaluator
queue "Kafka\nalerts" as Alerts
participant "Express API" as API
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Kafka -> Correlation : consume position event\n{ entity_id, lat, lon, timestamp_ms }

Correlation -> Redis : HGETALL entity:live:*\n(fetch all current positions)
Redis --> Correlation : positions of all live entities

Correlation -> Correlation : compute pairwise distances\nflag pairs within PROXIMITY_THRESHOLD_METRES

alt two entities within threshold
  Correlation -> Neo4j : MATCH (a:Entity {id: $id_a})-[:KNOWN_ASSOCIATE]-(b:Entity {id: $id_b})\nRETURN b

  note over Neo4j
    Graph absence query.
    Checks for a KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge
    between the two entity nodes.
    Single traversal - not a table scan.
  end note

  alt no KNOWN_ASSOCIATE edge found
    Correlation -> Neo4j : MERGE PROXIMITY_EVENT edge\n(see graph-update diagram for full idempotency detail)

    note over Correlation
      Correlation Worker's job ends here.
      It writes proximity evidence to Neo4j.
      Alert emission belongs to the Alert Evaluator
      so that leader election (ADR-005) governs
      all alert output from one place.
    end note
  else prior relationship exists
    Correlation -> Correlation : routine proximity - no edge written
  end
end

== Alert Evaluator - runs on its own independent evaluation cycle ==

note over Evaluator
  Completely separate from the Correlation Worker.
  Polls Neo4j on each evaluation cycle
  to find unscheduled proximity evidence
  written since the last cycle.
end note

Evaluator -> Neo4j : query PROXIMITY_EVENT edges\nwithout KNOWN_ASSOCIATE within window
Neo4j --> Evaluator : unscheduled proximity pairs
Evaluator -> Alerts : publish to alerts\n{ type: UNSCHEDULED_PROXIMITY,\n  entity_a, entity_b,\n  location, distance_metres, timestamp_ms }

Alerts -> API : consume alert
API --> Dashboard : push alert over WebSocket
Dashboard --> Operator : proximity alert displayed

@enduml
